WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:06.100
Despite the MCU's raging success at adapting
their library of comic book stories to film,

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.100
not every one of their storylines is well-suited
to the silver screen.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.280
Some stories are too violent.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.800
Some are simply too controversial, or carry
unsettling undertones.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.320
And a few are just too dang weird for a mainstream
movie studio.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.040
Whatever the cause, don't expect to see these
tales unfold in the theater until everyone's

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.740
run entirely out of ideas—and even then,
don't hold your breath.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.320
The Ultimates

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:33.580
The Avengers borrows a lot from The Ultimates:
superheroes bickering among themselves, the

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:38.320
Hulk going on a rampage, and a largescale
alien invasion forcing the team to put their

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.480
differences aside and come together to save
the Earth are all part of the iconic story.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.720
And then there's the fact that MCU Nick Fury
is a dead-on duplicate of Ultimate Nick Fury.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.640
So far, so good… but that's about as adaptable
as the Ultimates saga gets.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.880
The Ultimates presents a very cynical view
of superheroes.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.340
Ultimate Captain America is a xenophobe.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.360
Ultimate Hank Pym brutally beats his wife.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.260
Ultimate Hulk just straight-up eats people.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.680
Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver—brother and
sister—are lovers.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.039
Things reach an insane crescendo when the
X-Men villain the Blob eats the Wasp, and

00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:17.799
Hank Pym responds in kind, using his size-changing
abilities to get revenge by biting Blob's

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.300
head off.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.639
Most of the X-Men perish, Thing crushes Doctor
Doom's head with his bare hands, and Manhattan

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:24.940
is more or less annihilated.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.560
It goes without saying that the whole story
is too dour for mainstream Marvel to put on

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.060
the screen.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.120
People like to root for their heroes; The
Ultimates makes that more or less impossible.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.720
Secret Empire

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.240
You might've heard about the controversial
premise of Secret Empire, even if you're not

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:40.760
a comic reader.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.000
Yeah, that's right: this is the comic that
makes Captain America a Nazi.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.299
So, technically Cap was a sleeper agent for
HYDRA… except he wasn't really, thanks to

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.340
Red Skull and some Cosmic Cube stuff.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:57.119
But despite Marvel's claims, that doesn't
really make anything better... the basic story

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:02.600
is Steve Rogers infiltrates SHIELD, reveals
his true nature, and conquers America in HYDRA's

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.100
name.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.100
Isn't that uplifting?

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.600
Even if HYDRA-Cap isn't a Nazi by name, the
parallels are too strong to ignore.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.820
Because, you know, HYDRA is basically Nazis.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.320
Hail HYDRA

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.280
We've already had two HYDRA-fueled takeovers
of America in the MCU already, a third - led

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.720
by Nazi Cap - it's pretty unlikely.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.940
These days, real-life Nazis—some of whom
proudly wear Captain America's gear—are

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.200
an actual problem.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:33.560
Because of this, Secret Empire received plenty
of criticism from the comic book community.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.000
Marvel's not going to court that kind of controversy
by repeating the plot in theaters, and won't

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.840
risk tainting one of its most popular characters
for a stunt.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:42.780
Count on it.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.560
Sins Past

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:50.800
The Green Goblin might be Spider-Man's arch-nemesis,
but don't expect Norman Osborn to grace theater

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.020
screens any time soon.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.300
For the Goblin's diehard fans, that's bad
news, but there's one silver lining.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.820
Norman's absence means there's no way that
Spider-Man's "Sins Past" story arc will ever

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.820
get a big-screen adaptation, and that's very,
very good.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.360
"Sins Past" sees Peter Parker's girlfriend
Gwen Stacy have a brief fling with Norman,

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.840
the guy who eventually ends her life, while
vacationing in France.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.040
As a result of the encounter, Gwen gives birth
to twins.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.880
It's not only the age difference between Gwen
and Norman that makes the story so bad.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.800
It's not only that Mary Jane knew about the
affair and didn't tell Peter until the twins

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:27.680
appear at his door.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.020
No, it's that in the follow-up storyline,
"Sins Remembered," Peter makes out with one

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.820
of the twins because she kind of looks like
Gwen.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.900
Kissing the daughter of your long-lost love
and number one villain while you're married

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.680
to someone else?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.640
That's bad.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.280
Comic book readers didn't tolerate it, and
eventually, the whole affair was retconned

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.220
out of existence.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.060
Chances are, movie audiences wouldn't tolerate
it, either.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.460
Thor: Vikings

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:59.420
Not even Chris Hemsworth's dreamy smile and
strong sense of humor could make Thor: Vikings

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.320
work onscreen.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:05.400
As this dark superhero adventure reminds us,
the ancient Norsemen weren't wisecracking

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.860
swashbucklers like Thor and his comrades.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:13.160
They were hardened warriors with a mean streak
a mile long, which Thor: Vikings revels in.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:18.000
This is the comic that opens with a Viking
horde razing a Norwegian village, and then

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:22.789
sends the invaders to modern day New York,
where they pillage and slay their way through

00:04:22.789 --> 00:04:25.080
Manhattan as undead conquerors.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.520
They drive a spear through the mayor on live
television.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.540
They block the streets with piles of severed
heads.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:36.520
Even Thor has trouble stopping them, especially
after they snap both of the thunder god's

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:40.340
arms, chain his hammer to his neck, and chuck
him into the Hudson river.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.500
The differences between the violent, unforgiving
nature of real-life Vikings and colorful,

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.280
successful fare like Thor: Ragnarok are too
great.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.800
Even if it weren't, Thor: Vikings is just
too violent for mainstream moviegoers.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.220
Even dedicated gore-hounds might find some
of the gruesome antics stomach-turning.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.100
"That's a nice way of putting it."

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.120
Deadpool: Killustrated

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.520
Deadpool isn't an entirely bad guy, but he's
also got no problem with violence.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:11.320
He's a mercenary in a world full of supervillains,
so sometimes, gore is going to happen.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.240
It's just part of the job.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.700
That's why he's so popular.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.000
But there's still a line, and Deadpool's been
known to cross it.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:22.740
Not only has he obliterated every hero in
the Marvel Universe—twice—but in Deadpool:

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.440
Killustrated, the Merc with a Mouth hunts
down characters from pieces of classic literature.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.740
And yeah, it's kind of funny to watch Wade
Wilson scoop out Don Quixote's eyeballs, spread

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:37.360
Tom Sawyer's blood all over the boy's newly
painted fence, and torch Dracula.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.300
It's also very, very dark, even for Deadpool.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:45.380
On the page, Deadpool's violence doesn't seem
any worse than a particularly depraved cartoon.

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:50.360
Translate that story into live action, however,
and the murder of everyone in The Jungle Book

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.980
would be positively traumatic.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.080
JLA/Avengers

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.620
The Avengers proved that superhero crossovers
could work just as well in theaters as they

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:00.960
do in comic shops.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.840
But, these days, interconnected superhero
universes are old news.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:10.300
In fact, there's only one big superhero crossover
left to do, but it'll never happen.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:16.060
Letting DC and Marvel characters share the
same screen would be like the USS Enterprise

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.880
dogfighting with the Millennium Falcon.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.779
The corporate overlords at Disney and Warner
Bros. won't ever agree to it, even if fans

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.729
would literally rip off their own arms to
see it happen.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.780
That's a shame, too, because comic books have
already given both studios the perfect template

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:31.520
for a blockbuster.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:37.800
JLA/Avengers tells the story of an epic clash
between Earth's mightiest heroes and the League,

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.980
who duke it out before teaming up to stop
a timeless evil.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.920
JLA/Avengers could be the superhero movie
to end all superhero movies.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.280
But it won't be.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:51.300
Not only would the rights be a nightmare to
untangle, but after a team-up like that, there's

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.100
nowhere to go but down.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:53.540
Thanks for watching!

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.260
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

